Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in your `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => {
            // App lost focus (partially visible)
        })
        .OnStop(activity => {
            // App fully backgrounded
        }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => {
            // App entered background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- **Android `OnPause`** maps to the cross-platform `Deactivated` event (lost focus, may still be visible).
- **Android `OnStop`** and **iOS `DidEnterBackground`** both map to the cross-platform `Stopped` event (fully backgrounded).

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need the native callback signatures, you can simply use the `Window.Stopped` event — it fires on both platforms when the app backgrounds:

```csharp
// In App.cs
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
{
    var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);
    window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* save state here */ };
    return window;
}
```

> ⚠️ Keep handlers fast (<2 seconds) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS. On Android, also handle `OnDestroy` — the back button can skip `OnStop` entirely.
